nd $c$ are constants. Suppose that $r$, $s$, and $t$ are the roots of $P(x)$, and $r-2$, $s+5$, and $t-1$ are the roots of $Q(x)$. Find all possible values of $c$.\n\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within $\\boxed{}$.\n```\n\n## 解答\n\n利用韦达定理，我们有：\n\n对于 $P(x) = x^3 + ax^2 + bx + c$，其根为 $r, s, t$，则有：\n\\[ r + s + t = -a \\]\n\\[ rs + rt + st = b \\]\n\\[ rst = -c \\]\n\n对于 $Q(x) = x^3 + ax^2 + bx + c + 120$，其根为 $r-2, s+5, t-1$，则有：\n\\[ (r-2) + (s+5) + (t-1) = -a \\]\n\\[ (r-2)(s+5) + (r-2)(t-1) + (s+5)(t-1) = b \\]\n\\[ (r-2)(s+5)(t-1) = -(c+120) \\]\n\n通过上述方程，我们可以求解出 $c$ 的值。具体解法如下：\n\n1. 根据 $P(x)$ 的根关系，有 $r + s + t = -a$，则可以得到 $-a = -(r - 2 + s + 5 + t - 1)$，从而 $a = r - s - t + 4$。\n2. 又有 $rs + rt + st = b$，而 $Q(x)$ 的根为 $r-2, s+5, t-1$，则 $b = (r-2)(s+5) + (r-2)(t-1) + (s+5)(t-1)$。\n3. 最后利用 $rst = -c$ 和 $-(c+120) = (r-2)(s+5)(t-1)$，可以解得 $c$ 的值。\n\n综上所述，$c$ 的可能值为 $\\boxed{-120}$.",
